Fix three boolean settings that could not be turned off. Each reached a jinja template through `os.environ`, where every value is a string -- and `"False"` is a non-empty string, which jinja reads as true. `DEFER_ON_TLS_ERROR=False` left `smtp_tls_dane_insecure_mx_policy` at `dane` and `strict_testing` at `true` in the postfix container; `ADMIN=false`, which is what the setup wizard writes when the admin interface is disabled, still gave the webmail a Mailu button and a support link pointing at the admin UI that nginx does not route; and `FULL_TEXT_SEARCH_ATTACHMENTS=False` still configured dovecot's tika decoder. The admin container read all of these correctly, so a deployment that turned one off got inconsistent behaviour between containers. Also fix a `NameError` that replaced the error message for an unusable `PROXY_PROTOCOL` entry, such as a list written with spaces after the commas, with a traceback at container start.
